*> Test of the loot function set_potion (26 section 7.3; lane itemcomp, T9609): it sets potion_contents (53) to the potion named by "id" (with or without minecraft:),
*> a name that is no potion leaves the stack alone. Run through LOOT-MODIFIER on the item modifiers of core/tests/fixtures/loot.
 IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
 PROGRAM-ID. TEST-LOOT-POTION.
 DATA DIVISION.
 WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.
 COPY TESTLIB.
 COPY CORESTATE.
 COPY COREAPI.
 COPY CONTENT.
 COPY CSTACK.
 COPY LOOTCTX.
 01 WS-DIR                 PIC X(1100) VALUE "core/tests/fixtures/loot".
 01 WS-STATUS              BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-KEY                 PIC X(112).
 01 WS-ITEM                BINARY-LONG VALUE 0.
 01 WS-COUNT               BINARY-LONG VALUE 1.
 01 WS-HANDLE              BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-FOUND               BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-POTION              BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-HAS-COLOR           BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-COLOR               BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-CUSTOM              BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-I                   BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-NAMES.
    05 FILLER PIC X(24) VALUE "m_potion".
    05 FILLER PIC X(24) VALUE "m_potion_bare".
    05 FILLER PIC X(24) VALUE "m_potion_unknown".
 01 WS-N REDEFINES WS-NAMES.
    05 WS-NAME PIC X(24) OCCURS 3 TIMES.
 01 WS-WANT.
    05 FILLER BINARY-LONG VALUE 25.
    05 FILLER BINARY-LONG VALUE 5.
    05 FILLER BINARY-LONG VALUE -1.
 01 WS-W REDEFINES WS-WANT.
    05 WS-EXPECT BINARY-LONG OCCURS 3 TIMES.
 PROCEDURE DIVISION.
     CALL "TEST-SETTINGS" USING CORE-SETTINGS
     CALL "TEST-OPEN-WORLD" USING CORE-SETTINGS
     CALL "LOOT-LOAD" USING WS-DIR WS-STATUS
     MOVE "N" TO TL-MODE
     PERFORM VARYING WS-I FROM 1 BY 1 UNTIL WS-I > 3
         INITIALIZE LOOT-CONTEXT
         MOVE 0 TO WS-HANDLE
         MOVE SPACES TO WS-KEY
         STRING "test:" FUNCTION TRIM(WS-NAME(WS-I)) DELIMITED BY SIZE INTO WS-KEY
         CALL "LOOT-MODIFIER" USING WS-KEY LOOT-CONTEXT WS-ITEM WS-COUNT WS-HANDLE WS-FOUND
         CALL "SC-POTION-GET" USING WS-HANDLE WS-POTION WS-HAS-COLOR WS-COLOR WS-CUSTOM
         MOVE SPACES TO TL-CASE
         STRING "test loot potion " FUNCTION TRIM(WS-NAME(WS-I)) " sets the potion id" DELIMITED BY SIZE INTO TL-CASE
         MOVE WS-EXPECT(WS-I) TO TL-EXPECTED-N
         MOVE WS-POTION TO TL-OBSERVED-N
         CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     END-PERFORM
     STOP RUN.
 END PROGRAM TEST-LOOT-POTION.
 COPY CORETEST.
